# NativeOrchestrator demo requests. Start SQL Server (docker compose up -d) and the app (dotnet run), then send
# each request with VS Code's REST Client or Visual Studio. Every start returns a statusUrl: poll it until the saga's
# status is Completed, Compensated or Failed. The simulated systems' trigger values are in Simulated/SimulatedTriggers.cs.

@host = http://localhost:5080

### Customer onboarding: succeeds (identity check takes ~10 s)
# @name onboarding
POST {{host}}/sagas/customer-onboarding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "correlationId": "customer-1001",
  "data": { "customerName": "Ada Lovelace", "email": "ada@example.test" }
}

### Status
GET {{host}}{{onboarding.response.body.$.statusUrl}}

### History
GET {{host}}{{onboarding.response.body.$.statusUrl}}/history

### Same correlation ID again: returns the existing saga ("created": false)
POST {{host}}/sagas/customer-onboarding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "correlationId": "customer-1001",
  "data": { "customerName": "Ada Lovelace", "email": "ada@example.test" }
}

### Identity rejected: the reserved account is deleted (status Compensated)
# @name rejected
POST {{host}}/sagas/customer-onboarding
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "customerName": "REJECT Grace Hopper", "email": "grace@example.test" } }

###
GET {{host}}{{rejected.response.body.$.statusUrl}}

### Identity never verified: the step times out after 1 minute in Development (Compensated, StepTimedOut)
# @name slow
POST {{host}}/sagas/customer-onboarding
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "customerName": "SLOW Alan Turing", "email": "alan@example.test" } }

###
GET {{host}}{{slow.response.body.$.statusUrl}}

### Cancel it while it waits (status Compensated, Cancelled)
POST {{host}}{{slow.response.body.$.statusUrl}}/cancel

### Flaky accounts API (503 twice): the resilience handler retries inside the call; the saga doesn't notice
# @name flaky
POST {{host}}/sagas/customer-onboarding
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "customerName": "Barbara Liskov", "email": "flaky-barbara@example.test" } }

###
GET {{host}}{{flaky.response.body.$.statusUrl}}

### Welcome email bounces: the step has ContinueOnError, so the saga still completes
# @name bounce
POST {{host}}/sagas/customer-onboarding
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "customerName": "Edsger Dijkstra", "email": "edsger@bounce.test" } }

###
GET {{host}}{{bounce.response.body.$.statusUrl}}

### Invalid data: 400
POST {{host}}/sagas/customer-onboarding
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "customerName": "", "email": "nobody" } }

### Unknown saga type: 404
POST {{host}}/sagas/unknown
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": {} }

### Report generation: polls until the report is built (20 s here; hours in real life), then emails the link.
# report-generation is single-instance: wait for each report to finish before starting the next one.
# @name report
POST {{host}}/sagas/report-generation
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "correlationId": "monthly-sales-2026-10",
  "data": { "reportName": "Monthly sales", "recipients": ["finance@example.test"], "durationSeconds": 20 }
}

###
GET {{host}}{{report.response.body.$.statusUrl}}

### Another report while the first is still building: 409, outcome AlreadyRunning, with the running saga's ID
POST {{host}}/sagas/report-generation
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "reportName": "Daily sales", "recipients": ["finance@example.test"], "durationSeconds": 5 } }

### Report fails to build (status Compensated)
# @name failedReport
POST {{host}}/sagas/report-generation
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "reportName": "FAIL Quarterly", "recipients": ["finance@example.test"], "durationSeconds": 5 } }

###
GET {{host}}{{failedReport.response.body.$.statusUrl}}

### Report built, but the email bounces: the report is discarded (compensation), status Compensated
# @name bouncedReport
POST {{host}}/sagas/report-generation
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "reportName": "Weekly churn", "recipients": ["cfo@bounce.test"], "durationSeconds": 5 } }

###
GET {{host}}{{bouncedReport.response.body.$.statusUrl}}

### Emails the simulated notification system has sent
GET {{host}}/simulated/notifications/email

### Health (checks the saga database)
GET {{host}}/health
